class MalformedPackageTests(unittest.TestCase):
    """Round-15: the package checker names malformed packages;
    it must never crash on one. A record that parses as JSON but
    lacks the fields the recomputations index (an observation
    with no outcome, a text elapsed time, a pricing record with
    no rep or a null elapsed time) previously raised KeyError /
    TypeError out of check_run_package, hiding every check after
    the crash — the round-14 P1 defect class in its parseable
    form. The same round: recorded claims with an in-package
    anchor are verified — plan_counts against the configured
    plan's derived counts, slots_planned against the recorded
    order's own length, and each claim ledger entry's basis
    against the basis the records and recorded decisions give
    (previously a basis forged identically in claim-ledger.json
    and run.json passed clean, and a forged plan passed clean).

    Round-16: the same crash class on the remaining shape axes,
    plus the shapes that passed silently. The manifest itself was
    trusted to be an object (a run.json holding a JSON list,
    string, number or null raised AttributeError out of the
    checker); the recorded fingerprints were trusted to be
    per-arm objects carrying a string sha256 (a string, list or
    non-string sha256 raised out of the pricing provenance
    recomputation); a claim whose dimension was not a string
    raised TypeError in the ledger's dimension sort; a pricing
    record whose probe name was unhashable (a list, a dict)
    raised TypeError in the stamp cross-check; and a recorded
    identity list holding non-strings raised AttributeError in
    the outcome recomputation. On the silent side, an elapsed_ms
    of NaN, infinity or a negative number — each parses as a
    JSON number, none is a time the runner's monotonic clock can
    produce — passed every check and entered medians and paired
    differences unnamed, and an outcome string outside the five
    classifications the runner writes fed no median and no loss
    list, vanishing silently. Every shape below is now named,
    and a non-finite or negative pricing time prices nothing.

    Round-17: the next axes of the same class. Inside the
    pricing records, the containers themselves: an ok record
    missing its probe or shape raised KeyError out of the
    pairing (and out of check_run_package itself), and an
    unhashable rep raised TypeError out of the paired-count
    recomputation on the report path. The report path
    (cmd_report) applied no shape validation at all, so
    observation records the checker names — a missing arm, a
    text elapsed time, an unhashable rep — raised out of the
    render instead. And the manifest's recorded counts were
    compared by equality alone, so a count carried as a float
    (46.0 standing losses, 40.0 slots planned) passed unnamed
    where the same count as a string was named.

    Round-18: the class hunted as a class, by systematic
    type-flip mutation of every field of the preserved package
    through both consumers (checker and report). The render's
    own manifest fields were still unvalidated (a manifest
    missing plan_counts, or with fingerprints / platform /
    arm_versions / order in other shapes, crashed cmd_report
    while the checker tolerated the package); a non-string
    config_path crashed the identity recomputation; the
    round-17 integer rule stopped one level above plan_counts'
    fields and never reached the recorded order's repetitions;
    pricing provenance floored the paired count but never
    anchored the per-probe total to the run shape, so extra
    records the run never made priced; the pricing shape check
    read only "ok" records, though every record carries the
    stamp fields; and a fingerprint object without its sha256
    silently dropped out of the provenance stamp set."""

    def evidence_ns(self, tmp):
        src = os.path.normpath(
            os.path.join(HERE, "..", "evidence", "reduced-run"))
        dst = os.path.join(tmp, "reduced-run")
        shutil.copytree(src, dst)
        return dst

    def rewrite_jsonl(self, ns, name, mutate):
        path = os.path.join(ns, name)
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as handle:
            records = [json.loads(line) for line in handle
                       if line.strip()]
        mutate(records)
        with open(path, "w", encoding="utf-8") as handle:
            for record in records:
                handle.write(json.dumps(record) + "\n")

